Third party sources
ACE context packs restate facts published by governments, UN agencies,
research institutes, companies and news outlets. Each fact names its source,
and ACKNOWLEDGMENTS.md credits every organisation whose published work ACE
uses. Those sources keep their own rights and terms of use, and their names
and marks belong to their owners. A credit does not imply endorsement.

Language profiles
src/ace_engine/langid/profiles.json holds counts of three letter sequences,
derived in part from FLORES-200 by the NLLB Team at Meta AI, licensed under
CC BY-SA 4.0, and from translations of the Universal Declaration of Human
Rights published by OHCHR, through the UDHR in XML project. That file is
shared under CC BY-SA 4.0, not Apache 2.0:
https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/

